{
  "about": "Every game screen screens.look() recognises, by navigation.json id. A screen is the base (one at a time); an overlay shows over the bases it lists. Each anchor is a patch (a fixture's crop, or its box [x, y, w, h] in the crop's pixels, compared as a downscaled grey signature after its brightness and contrast are evened out: distance under limit), a share (the share of an area of screens.py passing a colour test, above or below a level) or a reader (a function returning true). An anchor's margin runs from 1 (sure) through 0 (its limit) to -1; a screen's margin is its anchors' lowest. status: registered (its fixtures are real crops and test_screen_model proves them) or measured (recognised from areas measured on a real capture that is not in fixtures yet: matched only when no registered screen is). Every other navigation.json screen is pending capture: never matched, and named in docs/TODO.md's calibration list. fixtures: the crops that, pasted back on an empty screen of background, make the screen; an overlay's include its base's.",
  "outside": {
    "account_chooser": "Android's window, told by dumpsys",
    "crash_dialog": "Android's window, told by dumpsys",
    "anr_dialog": "Android's window, told by dumpsys",
    "unknown": "the name of any screen not recognised"
  },
  "screens": {
